            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
            of chosen oriented points on their boundary, at least one on each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
            (
            %a{:href => "#BarNatan95"}> Bar-Natan 95, Def. 1.12
            ).
          %p
            A
            %em stringy weight system
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            from this space to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual vector space
          #eq:SpaceOfStringyWeightSystems.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                  %mi Span
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi MarkedSurfaces
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{S}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\Big(
                  Span\big( MarkedSurfaces_{/\sim} \big)
                  \\Big)^\ast
                  \\,.
          %p
            Of course a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Span
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi MarkedSurfaces
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔽
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span\big( MarkedSurfaces_{/\sim}\big) \to \mathbb{F}
            is equivalently a plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MarkedSurfaces
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝔽
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MarkedSurfaces \to \mathbb{F}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combinations"} formal linear combinations
            of marked surfaces:
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+double+line+construction"} 't Hooft double line construction
            constitutes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} linear span
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagrams"} Jacobi diagrams
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+vector+space"} modulo
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/STU-relations"} STU-relations
            to the linear span of marked surfaces
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LinearSpanOfMarkedSurfaces"} (1)
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AtHooftConstrictionIII.jpg", :width => "650"}/
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BarNatan95"}> Bar-Natan 95, Theorem 10 with Theorem 8
            )
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %p
            Under passage to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+spaces"} dual vector spaces
            this yields a linear map
          #eq:PointParticleLimitOfStringyWeightSystems.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi tH
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∘
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi perm
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒲
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{S}
                  \\overset{
                  (tH \,\circ\, perm)^\ast
                  }{\longrightarrow}
                  \\underset{n \in \mathbb{N}}{\prod}
                  \\big(
                  \\mathcal{W}^n
                  \\big)
          %p
            from stringy weight systems
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SpaceOfStringyWeightSystems"} (2)
            to ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldline+formalism"} point particle limit
            of stringy weight systems.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_lie_algebra_weight_systems Relation to Lie algebra weight systems
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stringy+weight+systems+span+classical+Lie+algebra+weight+systems"}> stringy weight systems span classical Lie algebra weight systems
                )
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SpaceOfStringyWeightSystems"} (2)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stringy+weight+systems"} stringy weight systems
              under the point particle limit map
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PointParticleLimitOfStringyWeightSystems"} (3)
              inside the space of ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
              coincides with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of the linear span of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+systems"} Lie algebra weight systems
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+Lie+algebras"} general linear Lie algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤𝔩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{gl}(N)
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+Lie+algebras"} special orthogonal Lie algebras
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔰𝔬
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(N)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+algebras"} symplectic Lie algebras
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔰𝔭
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sp}(N)
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/StringyWeightsSpanClassicalLieAlgebraWeight.jpg", :width => "450"}/
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BarNatan95"}> Bar-Natan 95, Theorem 11
            )
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+double+line+notation"} 't Hooft double line notation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory+as+a+topological+string+theory"} Chern-Simons theory as a topological string theory
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagrams"} chord diagrams
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+chord+diagrams"}> linear chord diagrams
                    ,
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/round+chord+diagrams"} round chord diagrams
                    %br/
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagrams"} Jacobi diagrams
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+chord+diagrams"} Sullivan chord diagrams
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+systems"}> Lie algebra weight systems
                    ,
                    %br/
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stringy+weight+system"} stringy weight system
                    %br/
